Essential navigation rules
The landing page must be publicly accessible.
The login portal must be a separate page.
Selecting a login role must open that role's dedicated login form.
After successful authentication, redirect the user to the correct dashboard.
All feature links must open their corresponding feature pages.
Clicking a feature must never redirect an authenticated user to the landing page.
Clicking the logo inside an authenticated workspace must not accidentally sign the user out or redirect them to the public landing page.
The authenticated workspace must maintain its role-specific navigation and layout while the user moves between features.
Only the explicit Sign Out action should normally end the authenticated session.
If a user manually opens the public landing page while authenticated, they may view the public page, but their session must remain active. The application should provide an appropriate link back to their dashboard.
Protected pages must remain protected when accessed directly through their URLs.
Refreshing a protected page must not unexpectedly sign the user out.
After signing out, protected pages must no longer be accessible without authentication.

Use a proper routing system. Do not implement the application as a single page where every feature button returns to the landing page.

