Routing rules
An unauthenticated visitor opening a protected route must be redirected to login.
After login, return the user to the originally requested page only if their role is authorized to access it.
Otherwise, send them to their correct dashboard.
Refreshing a valid protected page must preserve the authenticated session.
Moving between features must not reset authentication.
A user must not be able to open another role's dashboard by manually typing its URL.
Invalid routes must show an appropriate not-found page.
Expired sessions must be handled safely.
Signing out must clear private client-side state and redirect to the landing page.

Never rely solely on frontend route guards. Protect the underlying API and data as well.

